<id/05/0568/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Baskets"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_glass_ceramics_paper_woodware/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a vessel made of twigs, oslers, or rushes, and used for the stowage or conveyance of merchandise, tools, &c. In the East, all sort of basket-work is made of split cane; baskets are also made of the date palm. In Burmah and Arracan, the basket is the common dry measure for rice, and it weighs from 55 $\\frac{1}{2}$ to 58 $\\frac{1}{2}$ lbs., [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 40]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0568" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Baskets"@en ;
